{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You shall kindle no fire throughout your settlements on the sabbath day.</b> He singled out kindling from the general category — either in order to permit kindling in the Sanctuary and to say that only 'throughout your settlements' you shall not kindle, but in the Sanctuary it is permitted to kindle (Shabbat 20a); or in order that one should not say: just as He forbade us all the labors of our own homes also in the Temple, so too what is permitted in the Temple is permitted also in the home — therefore it makes known to us: 'You shall not kindle' establishes a paradigm for all the labors of the Tabernacle: even though they are permitted there, none the less they are forbidden 'throughout your settlements.'" "And by way of allusion, he alludes here to the punishment of those who profane the Sabbath, as is found in the chapter Kol Kitvei (Shabbat 119b): Rav said: Fire is found only in a place of Sabbath profanation, as it is said (Jeremiah 17:27), 'If you do not heed Me to hallow the sabbath day… I will kindle a fire in her gates and it shall devour the palaces of Jerusalem and it shall not be quenched.' Rav Naḥman bar Yitzḥak said: At an hour when people are not available to extinguish it. Rashi explained: that is, on the Sabbath. And this is what it says here: 'whoever does any work on it shall be put to death,' and it says <b>you shall kindle no fire</b> — do not cause for yourselves, by failing to keep the Sabbath as is fitting, that fire blaze <b>throughout your settlements</b>, in your roofed houses, <b>on the sabbath day</b>, at an hour when people are not available to extinguish it. See all of this in Ollot Efrayim, discourse 261."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {1 "The clause beginning קָא מַשְׁמַע לָן and the phrase בָּנָה אָב are rendered according to the Talmudic逻辑 of בניין אב (establishing a paradigm); the syntax of this second alternative is compressed in the original and I have unpacked it minimally to preserve the argumentative thread."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:20.794289186Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}